\item \textbf{(Sample and alphabet.)} \(n,d\in\mathbb N\) satisfy \(n\ge 1\) and \(d\ge 1\).
\item \textbf{(Overlap.)} The overlap parameter \(\epsilon\in\mathbb R\) satisfies \(0<\epsilon<1/2\).
\item \textbf{(Collision regime.)} The dimensions satisfy \(d\le n^2\).
\end{itemize}
Let \(\mathcal H_{n,d}^{\mathrm{bin}}(\epsilon)\) denote the fixed-sample binary exactly homogeneous source experiment: its sampling law is the \(n\)-fold independent experiment generated by binary laws with uniform cell masses on the \(d\) cells, propensities in \([\epsilon,1-\epsilon]\), and a common cell effect across all cells.  Then the minimax mean-squared risk for estimating the binary average response contrast \(\psi(P)\) satisfies
\[
\frac{u_{\epsilon}^2}{64}\frac{d}{n^2}
\le
\inf_{\widehat\psi}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal H_{n,d}^{\mathrm{bin}}(\epsilon)}
E_{P^{\otimes n}}\!\left[\{\widehat\psi-\psi(P)\}^2\right],
\]
where the infimum ranges over all measurable real-valued estimators \(\widehat\psi\) of the \(n\)-sample.
